X:1
T:Rhyfeddod ar Foreuddydd
T:A Marvel at Daybreak
R:carol
S:https://amgueddfa.cymru/casgliadau/caneuongwerin/?id=11 (collected by D. Roy Saer)
N:Sung by John Roberts (born 1901), a farmer, of Cerddin, Llanymawddwy, Meirionnydd; recorded 25.6.63, verses 1 and 2 only (St Fagans tape 625). A Christmas carol of the Perthyfelin family of Dinas Mawddwy: he learnt it around 1925-33 from hearing it sung by two of his uncles, brothers of Dafydd Roberts, "Telynor Mawddwy". The family called the tune "Cwplws Dau" (Couple Two). The words were kept in family notebooks, which name the author as William Edwards, Cae Coch, perhaps William Edwards (1806-69) of Cae Coch, Rhyd-y-main, near Dolgellau. After the first two verses the carol turns from the Nativity to the miracles, the Crucifixion and what followed, and ends with the customary call to repentance.
N:The singer slowed down every time he sang bar 3. The C in bars 25 and 35 has a bracketed sharp on the score: he sang it as C, C sharp or somewhere between. The two quavers on "gain" in bar 32 are in brackets on the score and are left out in verses 2 and 3 ("gain" may well be a later addition to verse 1).
